# ================================================================================
# Title: Disequilibrium Carbon, Oxygen, and Nitrogen Chemistry in the
#        Atmospheres of HD 189733b and HD 209458b
# Authors: Moses J.I., Visscher C., Fortney J.J., Showman A.P., Lewis N.K.,
#          Griffith C.A., Klippenstein S.J., Shabram M., Friedson A.J.,
#          Marley M.S., Freedman R.S.
# ================================================================================
# Description of contents: The tar package contains five ascii output files
#  from model runs described in the paper.  Each file contains a list of species
#  in the model; a list of reactions (without rate coefficients -- those are
#  found later in the file for reaction numbers provided in this list); the
#  background atmospheric temperature, pressure, density, and eddy diffusion
#  coefficients at the grid points; assumed kinetic rate coefficients at
#  those grid points (see also the Supplementary Table S1); and model results
#  for species concentrations, volume mixing ratios (mole fractions), production
#  and loss rates; photolysis rates (s^-1); reaction rates for all reactions
#  in the model (e.g., the reaction rate for reaction number x, described by
#  A + B = C + D, is the rate coefficient k_x times the concentration of species
#  A times the concentration of species B); and chemical loss time scales for
#  the species.  Units are cgs unless otherwise indicated.  The ascii files are
#  fully viewable and searchable with any text editor; headings for the different
#  categories of output typically end with a colon to aid the searches.  The file
#  names contain the name of the planet (hd189 = HD 189733b; hd209 = HD 209458b),
#  a shorthand for the thermal structure ("termave" is terminator average, "wtday"
#  and "dayave" are dayside averages, and "1d2pi" is the 1-D thermal structure
#  for the assumption that the incident stellar energy is redistributed over the
#  dayside hemisphere only), and a description of the K_zz profile for the model.
#  All models provide in the tar file have the "nominal" K_zz profile estimated
#  for the particular temperature profile, as described in the text.
# 
# System requirements: Files can be read with any text editor on any operating
#  system.
# 
# Additional comments: Additional model output or model information available
#  upon request from the first author.
# 
# ================================================================================
# 
# 





## IMPORTANT INFORMATION (added by Junaid)
# For rate coefficients please check TableS1.pdf
# R1-137 are photolysis reactions




